  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5acf2cf32a9b1134ea7a8b6ad6b27ae6, type: 3}
  m_Name: DuckSpeaks
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuacxiconSO
  categories:
  - categoryName: DuckThoughts
    contentList:
    - "thinks no one should \nstands in John Quackna's\nway"
    - thinks it is so quacky
    - has been staring at a puddle for several minutes. He now believes the sky lives
      underground.
    - found a stick and briefly assumed he had become employed.
    - smelled a flower. He is uncertain whether it was a snack or an opinion.
    - walked into a rock with tremendous confidence. He has blamed the rock for moving.
    - spent the morning following a butterfly. He has learned nothing.
    - is attempting to intimidate a pebble. The pebble remains unmoved.
    - looked at his own footprint and became concerned that someone is stalking him.
    - has decided the wind is invisible soup.
    - tried to sit on water. The results were educational.
    - found a leaf. He is treating it like a legal document.
    - has become emotionally attached to a  rock.
    - watched a cloud for too long and now suspects it is thinking about him.
    - tried to eat the concept of distance.
    - is glaring at the sun. This rivalry will not end well.
    - heard an echo and assumed the world was politely quacking back.
    - spent ten minutes preparing to jump over nothing in particular.
    - has mistaken a shadow for a hole and is refusing to go near it.
    - is carrying a twig with the dignity of a decorated war hero.
    - looked into the pond and gasped. He appears to have discovered another duck
      again.
    - has concluded that mud is just wet floor seasoning.
    - is trying to remember where he was going. He has also forgotten where he currently
      is.
    - pecked a rock repeatedly in the hope that it would eventually become bread.
    - has been standing very still to see if thinking happens on its own.
    - believes the grass is growing specifically to annoy him.
    - saw two Crumbies at once and temporarily lost the ability to behave.
    - has decided a nearby bush is probably a university.
    - tried to whisper to a tree. The tree offered no guidance.
    - is deeply suspicious of the pound.
    - found a feather on the ground and is unsettled by the evidence.
    - has been chasing his own excitement in a small circle.
    - looked very hard at a nest and concluded that architecture is mostly luck.
    - is trying to smell whether rain is approaching. He currently smells like dirt.
    - has confused bravery with poor judgment once again.
    - watched another duck trip and seems inspired.
    - is treating a very ordinary rock like a historical landmark.
    - has developed a personal philosophy based entirely on crumbies.
    - is unsure why his feet keep taking him places, but he appreciates their initiative.
    - has attempted to organize three pebbles into a family.
    - believes the pond is larger on the inside.
    - has taken a short break from doing nothing to do something worse.
    - is investigating whether silence is edible.
    - has decided that being lost is just a scenic route.
    - found a patch of dirt and seems convinced it contains secrets.
    - is waiting for a stick to do something impressive.
    - has become tired from thinking and will now resume not thinking.
    - tried to inspect a flower up close and sneezed directly into destiny.
    - is staring at the horizon like he personally misplaced it.
    - smelled his own feathers. He has decided he smells like a damp sponge.
    - bought a ticket for QQE super slang.
    sourceTxtFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: d1cb3245eed4bbf48af73be6264493e2, type: 3}
    targetCategoryName: DuckThoughts
    clearExistingContent: 0
